Dear Hiring Team,

It is with great pleasure that I submit my candidacy for the *Software Engineer* position with *Western Digital*. I bring over three years of professional experience building backend systems, cloud-agnostic storage services, and data pipelines, along with a strong academic foundation as a Master of Science in Computer Science graduate from Pace University, NY.

Through my experience across two engineering roles, I have designed, developed, tested, and improved software that directly reflects *the systems-level engineering depth this position demands*. As a Software Engineer at Sperse, I designed and developed system software and internal engineering tools in Python, LangGraph, and FastAPI serving 10,000+ users, and built GitHub Actions CI/CD pipelines with Docker to troubleshoot, debug, and optimize software performance before every production release. I engineered a FastMCP server exposing 160+ backend actions with built-in monitoring, writing clean, efficient, and maintainable code that automated workflows securely across multiple customers. Prior to Sperse, as a Software Engineer at Qualitest, I designed a cloud-agnostic Storage Service in Java and Spring Boot with PostgreSQL and Redis that handled file uploads, downloads, and deletions across S3, Google Cloud Storage, and MinIO via expiring signed URLs — giving me direct, hands-on experience with the storage systems and cloud infrastructure at the heart of Western Digital's work. I also optimized PostgreSQL with window functions, materialized views, and indexing to improve query latency and scalability, exposed the results through interactive React dashboards for stakeholders, and built data pipelines orchestrating long-running jobs with AWS Step Functions to improve error recovery across 100K+ weekly executions. Together, these roles have prepared me to *collaborate across engineering teams to build reliable, high-performance systems* and drive impact within a fast-moving engineering organization.

My academic and project experience has sharpened my foundation in distributed systems, debugging, and performance analysis — skills that translate directly into *the engineering rigor and collaborative culture this team values*. In my Dark Factory project, I built a distributed coding-agent orchestrator that decomposes large requests into dependency-aware task DAGs and executes them across multiple machines with retries and timeout handling, work that demanded careful reasoning about system-level reliability, concurrency, and failure recovery. This experience shaped me into an engineer who builds with rigor, communicates clearly across teams, and validates with evidence — qualities I would bring to Western Digital's early career engineering team.

I have always been passionate about *building the storage infrastructure behind hyperscale data centers and the AI-driven data economy*, and envision myself contributing my talent to the furthering of *Western Digital's mission to store, manage, and unlock the potential of the world's data at real scale*. I would love to discuss my interest in this position with your team and can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration, I look forward to connecting!

